# Evolution keeps its own libraries in a private directory of its own
# (privlibdir, /usr/lib/evolution) rather than on the loader's default
# search path, so a module that dlopens libevolution-mail.so/
# libevolution-shell.so has to record that directory in its own RUNPATH or
# it cannot load at all outside a process that already has them resident —
# every module Evolution installs under /usr/lib/evolution/modules/*.so
# already carries exactly this RUNPATH, this one included. lintian's
# custom-library-search-path tag still fires on it, because its exemption
# for a package's own private libdir only matches /usr/lib/<source-package>,
# which this is not; since the RUNPATH itself is required for the module to
# load, the fix is this override arguing the entry is deliberate, not
# removing the RUNPATH.
evolution-jmap: custom-library-search-path RUNPATH /usr/lib/evolution [usr/lib/evolution/modules/module-jmap-configuration.so]
